This product includes original skill guidance, two deterministic scripts
(PubMed incremental fetching and digest rendering with an anti-plagiarism
gate), and evaluation artifacts released under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

PubMed citation metadata retrieved during real runs originates from the
NCBI E-utilities service and is used in accordance with the NCBI policies
(https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/home/about/policies/). Abstracts are
copyrighted by their publishers: committed run artifacts carry redacted
abstract fields, and digests contain only original one-line Chinese notes,
links, and metadata.

All evaluation fixtures (PMIDs 99010001-99010006, titles, authors, journals,
and abstracts) are synthetic and fabricated for testing; they do not point to
real papers. Products named in references/benchmarks.md identify sources of
design lessons only; nothing from them is redistributed in this repository.
